    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0366" n="354" xml:id="pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Bulgaria)/10–2745:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative in Bulgaria</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-27T00:00:00+02:00">October 27,
                            1945—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received October 28—6:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>642. General Crane informed orally by General Biryusov Russian authorities will
                    not clear Dr. Black<anchor n="84" xml:id="d357-f1"/> into Bulgaria. He said
                    Black not sufficiently friendly to Russian objectives here. Do not believe we
                    should acquiesce this unjustifiable attitude. Recommend vigorous protest both
                    here and Moscow. Think it significant Biryusov has not put his views in
                    writing.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Istanbul as No. 8.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Barnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d357-f1" n="84" xml:id="d357-f1-content">
                <p>Floyd H. Black, president, American College, Sofia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
